# SSDF M1 — vSRX stream-mode security logging onboarding.
# Applied to a vSRX via rust-junosmcp (load_and_commit_config).
#
# REQUIREMENT: the device clock MUST be UTC. SSDF parses syslog timestamps as
# naive UTC; a non-UTC device skews ssdf.events.timestamp (see the P2 paloalto
# +4h backfill, infra/clickhouse/012_backfill_paloalto_utc.sql.example).
# Junos defaults to UTC when `system time-zone` is unset — verify before
# onboarding with `show system uptime` (expect "Current time: ... UTC") and do
# NOT set a non-UTC `set system time-zone`.
# Verified 2026-06-12 on vsrx-br05: no time-zone configured, clock UTC.
# Substitutions (as-built 2026-06-06, vsrx-br05):
#   <srx-data-plane-ip> = 198.51.100.160  (ge-0/0/0.0 — stream logs source from the data plane, NOT fxp0)
#   <vector-host-ip>    = 198.51.100.150  (ssdf-vector LXC 102, UDP/514)
set security log mode stream
set security log source-address 198.51.100.160
set security log stream SSDF format sd-syslog
set security log stream SSDF category all
set security log stream SSDF severity info
set security log stream SSDF host 198.51.100.150 port 514
